nd that the apology enter the committee record.\"\n          },\n          \"specificity\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1's allotment committee nameplate and B2's result sheet establish an immediately playable meeting dispute.\"\n          },\n          \"brevityWit\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5's 'minute your apology' compresses the role claim and injured dignity into a consequence enabled by B4.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"hardGates\": {\n        \"fiveSpokenTurns\": true,\n        \"aHoldsRequestedCard\": true,\n        \"b2CausesA3\": true,\n        \"b4CausesA5\": true,\n        \"noSeparateNarration\": true,\n        \"noUnrelatedPunchline\": true,\n        \"noRealPartnerInstruction\": true,\n        \"noForcedEnding\": true\n      },\n      \"hardGateEvidence\": {\n        \"b2CausesA3\": \"A3 explicitly objects to B2's demand to prove entitlement to chair the meeting.\",\n        \"b4CausesA5\": \"B4 introduces the secretary call; A5 requests speakerphone and makes that secretary the prospective recorder of B's apology.\",\n        \"cardContribution\": \"A assumes rightful possession in A1 and interprets ordinary verification as an insult in A3 and A5.\",\n        \"sameGameHeightened\": \"A5 converts confirmation of authority into a proposed public remedy for questioning it; neither confirmation nor apology is forced to occur.\"\n      },\n      \"reservation\": \"A3 states the affront quite directly, and B's personal relationship to A remains thin. No rewrite needed.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The preserved founders' dinner alternative restores physical precedence after recognition. This committee alternative uses verification itself to demand a recorded apology.\",\n      \"accept\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S53-single-b\",\n      \"candidateHash\": \"19e3ddc20aafeb4eaeff82ae4780b95b029e3730d3242b9189bd0346c387