ce\": \"A1's bakery mixer, B2's birthday gift and B4's Friday bread tasting establish a clear personal-commercial boundary.\"\n          },\n          \"brevityWit\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"A5's 'I'll come Thursday' efficiently turns B4's friendly invitation into an attempt to preempt the customer vote.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 88\n      },\n      \"hardGates\": {\n        \"fiveSpokenTurns\": true,\n        \"aHoldsRequestedCard\": true,\n        \"b2CausesA3\": true,\n        \"b4CausesA5\": true,\n        \"noSeparateNarration\": true,\n        \"noUnrelatedPunchline\": true,\n        \"noRealPartnerInstruction\": true,\n        \"noForcedEnding\": true\n      },\n      \"hardGateEvidence\": {\n        \"b2CausesA3\": \"A3 answers B2's gift-versus-investment distinction by insisting that the gift constituted backing the business.\",\n        \"b4CausesA5\": \"B4 supplies the bread, the Friday date and the customer decision; A5 claims an earlier approval stage over those exact choices.\",\n        \"cardContribution\": \"The past mixer gift explains why A claims present influence, rather than merely wanting free samples.\",\n        \"sameGameHeightened\": \"A's claimed return on support grows from participation in A1 to veto power in A5.\"\n      },\n      \"reservation\": \"A3's tasting entitlement is comparatively mild; the jump to veto power in A5 is clear but abrupt. No rewrite needed.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The preserved club alternative treats repaid funding as lasting influence over naming. This alternative reclassifies a personal gift as investment and exploits an invitation to seize an earlier decision stage.\",\n      \"accept\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S57-single-a\",\n      \"candidateHash\": \"2975647e7248af06e12d1cd920c31d29f579cefc891056ace77c2b4666915340\",\n      \"secondPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n           